The '''fifth season''' (also known as '''''The Traitors: New Blood''''') of the American television series '''''[[The Traitors (American TV series)|The Traitors]]''''' was announced on June 18, 2026.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://deadline.com/2026/06/the-traitors-new-blood-premiere-date-nbc-civilian-series-1236959387/ | title='The Traitors: New Blood' Sets September Premiere Date On NBC For Civilian Series|date=June 18, 2026|access-date=12 August 2026}}</ref> The season premiered on September 17, 2026 on [[NBC]] with episodes releasing the next day on [[Peacock (streaming service)|Peacock]].

==Format==
The show retains the same [[The Traitors (American TV series)#Format|format]] and missions as the ''[[The Traitors UK]]'' and its US Celebrity counterpart. The contestants, all ordinary people from all across the US, are invited to the same castle in the Scottish Highlands to play this all-civilian version of the game. They are split into two particular Groups: the "Faithful," who are tasked with playing the game and trying to avoid banishment and/or murder to make it to the end of the game and win the final prize pot, and the "Traitors," a group of contestants secretly selected by host [[Alan Cumming]] who will work with the Faithful to build up the pot but are secretly working to earn the prize themselves. Most nights, the Traitors decide who to eliminate from the game via a "murder" while working to remain undetected and avoid suspicion from the other players. Each day the contestants participate in various missions to add money to the prize fund which can reach a maximum of $250,000. 

In this version there is an additional incentive: for every Traitor that is successfully banished from the game, the team will add an additional $15,000 to the prize fund. At the end of each day, the players participate in the Round Table, where they must decide who to banish from the game in the hope of identifying the Traitors.

If all remaining players are Faithful, the prize money is divided evenly among them. However, if even one Traitor remains, they win the entire pot.<ref>{{Cite web |last=SYFY Wire |date=April 29, 2022 |title=Peacock nabs psychological thriller competition 'The Traitors' hosted by 'Bond' vet Alan Cumming |url=https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/peacock-the-traitors-alan-cumming |access-date=January 13, 2023 |website=SYFY Wire |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=USA |date=December 7, 2022 |title=Alan Cumming Hosts Peacock's 'The Traitors' In Remote Scottish Castle – What To Know |url=https://www.usanetwork.com/usa-insider/alan-cumming-hosts-peacock-the-traitors-gameshow |access-date=January 13, 2023 |website=USA Network |language=en}}</ref>

== Contestants ==
[[File:Xavier Scruggs batting for the Memphis Redbirds in 2015 (Cropped).jpg|right|thumb|200px|[[Xavier Scruggs]]]]

Unlike the [[The Traitors (American TV series) season 4|previous seasons]], this seasons cast was composed entirely of civilian (not celebrity) participants. ''[[Entertainment Weekly]]'' announced the 22 cast members via social media on August 12, 2026.<ref name=Cast>{{cite web |title=The Traitors: New Blood first ever all-civilian cast revealed (exclusive) |url=https://ew.com/the-traitors-new-blood-first-ever-all-civilian-cast-revealed-exclusive-12056293|publisher=Entertainment Weekly |date=12 August 2026 |access-date=12 August 2026}}</ref>

In the first episode, Cumming revealed that two contestants would be recruited as "Accomplices". They would have to complete a series of tasks before the original Traitors would make a final decision on who would join them in the turret.

